#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42c41150-5104-58cc-927b-f55b94529cb2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Order of a Numerical Method By Comparing LTE for Different Step Sizes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2dd684e-b3ec-5155-8b84-cead6ecd77ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.019" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368718} {:answer/id #uuid "4383c669-3a39-5a9c-89a5-3a47a94e406d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.095" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368719} {:answer/id #uuid "357d9b13-23d1-53c3-a9ce-0ea2867cbb5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.350" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368720} {:answer/id #uuid "e4e3bb3a-5079-5c8a-9172-41d665140ecc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.175" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368721} {:answer/id #uuid "b2697abb-9b38-57d1-aca8-b546c1d10e12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.281" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2697abb-9b38-57d1-aca8-b546c1d10e12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.281" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368722} :answer-field/id #uuid "04eece3d-a2d6-5891-bcbf-9e883ab6b5f4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368717} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccbda39f-a3e7-56a4-a30b-a3bca7bed7fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.019" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368724} {:answer/id #uuid "0c6e74c4-b1b4-5a24-a70d-8a29aae238ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.095" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368725} {:answer/id #uuid "b080873b-0517-509c-85c8-692ab41610c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.350" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368726} {:answer/id #uuid "4c7695ef-cc34-558b-b584-d1dfaa97d918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.175" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368727} {:answer/id #uuid "42edc182-721d-5a0c-a3c6-32c7fad2a856" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.281" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccbda39f-a3e7-56a4-a30b-a3bca7bed7fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.019" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368724} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff74b603-44c9-5828-b2d7-37f6ba653ffd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368723} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16ae723c-c841-5d3e-8221-5f2aebe33816" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.500" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368730} {:answer/id #uuid "f224d79e-d340-562a-b619-5991c428ba30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.158" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368731} {:answer/id #uuid "28c50ae1-18ce-505b-963a-0c4f258e39e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.375" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368732} {:answer/id #uuid "67bf39e8-5415-5a33-be22-c755ac3c2d60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.640" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368733} {:answer/id #uuid "d57a6935-c624-5276-ae3d-a289c999b1e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.250" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f224d79e-d340-562a-b619-5991c428ba30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.158" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368731} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dd531bc-26f3-5e5d-9161-e869b241c4b4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368729} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd06c816-ed4d-59eb-92dc-09c8a85a28b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368736} {:answer/id #uuid "b8dfb9da-35e7-59ee-baf1-bb6dbd054214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368737} {:answer/id #uuid "ce240398-757e-5bbe-8666-2d8212a44702" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368738} {:answer/id #uuid "e639c766-c4dc-544b-8f1a-977c32a3759b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368739} {:answer/id #uuid "8b7ae534-6258-50d9-9da9-8918257ef516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd06c816-ed4d-59eb-92dc-09c8a85a28b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368736} :answer-field/id #uuid "42a6359a-27f7-567e-a79f-553a4d10ba82" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6acd5ad6-cecd-50bc-9edc-fc2a85e9b7ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-334652" :question/problem "The local truncation error (LTE) of a numerical method with step size $Δx$ is\n\n$$\nτ(Δx)=5(Δx)^{4}-(Δx)^{5}.\n$$\n\nComplete the following sentences.$\\,$ With step size $Δx=0.5,$ the local truncation error is $≈$\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ With step size $Δx=0.25,$ the local truncation error is $≈$\n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Decreasing from $Δx=0.5$ to $Δx=0.25,$ the LTE is reduced by a factor of $≈$\n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ According to this data, the order of the method is approximately\n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "A numerical method has order $p$ if $p$ is the largest positive integer such that the local truncation error (LTE) satisfies\n\n$$\nτ(Δx)=O\\,((Δx)^{p+1})\\,\\text{as}\\,Δx\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThe order describes how fast errors shrink as $Δx$ decreases.\n\nIn other words, a numerical method has order $p$ if, for sufficiently small step sizes, reducing the step size by a factor of $k$ reduces the LTE by a factor of approximately ${k}^{p+1}.$\n\nFirst, we compute the LTE for the given step sizes:\n\n- With step size $Δx=0.5,$ the LTE is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}τ(0.5) & =5(0.5)^{4}-(0.5)^{5} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 0.062\\,5-1\\cdot 0.031\\,25 \\\\  & =0.281\\,25 \\\\  & ≈0.281.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- With step size $Δx=0.25,$ the LTE is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}τ(0.25) & =5(0.25)^{4}-(0.25)^{5} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 0.003\\,90...-1\\cdot 0.000\\,97... \\\\  & =0.018\\,55... \\\\  & ≈0.019.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we determine the order by comparing the errors. The step size decreases from $0.5$ to $0.25.$ So, it reduces by a factor of\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{0.5}{0.25}=2.\n$$\n\nAs a result, for a numerical method of order $p,$ the LTE should decrease by a factor of approximately\n\n$$\n{k}^{p+1}={2}^{p+1}.\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, the LTE actually decreases from $0.281\\,25$ to $0.018\\,55....$ So, it reduces by a factor of\n\n$$\n\\frac{0.281\\,25}{0.018\\,55...}=15.157\\,89…≈15.158.\n$$\n\nComparing the two scale factors for the LTE, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{p+1} & ≈15.157\\,89… \\\\ p+1 & ≈{log}_{2}⁡(15.157\\,89…) \\\\ p+1 & ≈3.922… \\\\ p & ≈2.922….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, rounding to the nearest integer, the estimated order of the method is\n$3.$\n\nIndeed, this coincides with the definition of the order from the expression for the LTE:\n\n$$\nτ(Δx)=5(Δx)^{4}-(Δx)^{5}\\,⇒\\,τ(Δx)=O\\,((Δx)^{4})=O\\,((Δx)^{3+1}),\\,Δx\\to 0.\n$$\n\nHence, the order of the method is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368741 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42c41150-5104-58cc-927b-f55b94529cb2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Order of a Numerical Method By Comparing LTE for Different Step Sizes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ff11c9b-c433-5eac-9106-369e77a125f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368743} {:answer/id #uuid "a953d5aa-5044-5beb-8e46-34fb86d932e4" :answer/typ